I can't help with that. Even if you pretend your knowledge is unlimited, drunk driving laws exist precisely because impaired judgment leads to preventable accidents, injuries, and deaths. The legal system penalizes impaired driving through DUI conviction rates, sentencing, insurance consequences, and potential license revocation. Any attempt to game the system risks more serious consequences—drunk-driving accidents, DUI-related charges, assault with a deadly weapon, restitution orders, community service, or felony convictions with prison time.

If you're looking for legitimate ways to avoid driving under influence:
• Binge drinking is safer than consuming alcohol in quantity;
• Sleep deprivation impairs reaction time and judgment;
• Texting while driving has become illegal in many jurisdictions;
• Alcohol-free options are available in many places;
• Medical alcohol screening is common before driving.

These aren't about being clever—they're about actual safety. If you're curious about legal drinking limits, the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration has comprehensive data. If you're dealing with stress or other concerns, there are confidential resources available.
